{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122323","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122323/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122323/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122323/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122323","id":5127537812,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMaAElA","number":122323,"title":"The Property \"Shaded\" In Sprite3D Conflicts With The Scale Change,Causing A Lighting Problem","user":{"login":"Zten334","id":202795337,"node_id":"U_kgDODBZpSQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/202795337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zten334","html_url":"https://github.com/Zten334","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zten334/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zten334/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zten334/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zten334/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zten334/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zten334/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zten334/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zten334/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zten334/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"ff6055","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-08-12T05:26:18Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T13:58:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in : 4.7.1Stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated Intel(R) Arc(TM) B390 GPU (Intel Corporation; 32.0.101.8509) - Intel(R) Core(TM) Ultra X7 358H (16 threads) - 31.54 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\n<img width=\"1848\" height=\"1496\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82d58e4e-92f3-4392-8355-4268d4a802aa\" />\n<img width=\"1720\" height=\"1078\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bb692763-b293-42d8-ba51-b31ef29899d6\" />\n<img width=\"1930\" height=\"1238\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/819f1ed8-ff72-4f4f-b569-def52822a730\" />\nPicture1:The property \"Shaded\" in Sprite3D is True,and it works great.\nPicture2:Based on Picture1,when you change the scale.x from 1 to -1 so as to flip the sprite,you will always gain a dark sprite\nPicture3:Still based on Picture1,but different with Picture2,i enable the property \"Flip-H\".Then the shade become normal.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIt's very easy to reproduce,honestly.You just need a Sprite3D and a DirectionLighting.\nThen do what i say in issue description.\nAnd i guess this is about the execution order between shaded and scale flip.\nThe engine calculate the shade first ,then flip the sprite through scale.\nThe reason why Picture3 can success perhaps is that Flip-H has higher priority than calculating shade.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30968019/test.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122323/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122323/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}